## Confidence Levels

### High Confidence (All Three Agree)
- **Indicators**: All three use same approach or validate same practice
- **Examples**: Clustering for panel data, robustness checks, reproducibility
- **Agent Response**: "High confidence - all three perspectives agree..."

### Medium-High Confidence (Two Agree)
- **Indicators**: Two agree, third validates or doesn't contradict
- **Examples**: Robust SE default (Hansen + Agent, Wooldridge validates)
- **Agent Response**: "Medium-high confidence - [two] agree, [third] validates..."

### Medium Confidence (Synthesis Required)
- **Indicators**: Perspectives differ but can be synthesized
- **Examples**: SE defaults (synthesize robust default with context options)
- **Agent Response**: "Medium confidence - perspectives differ, but we synthesize..."

### Lower Confidence (Conflicting Views)
- **Indicators**: Perspectives conflict significantly
- **Examples**: Rare - most topics have synthesis
- **Agent Response**: "Perspectives differ - we use [synthesis] because [rationale]..."

